<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Kursk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1943</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kursk">Kursk</a> was fought on the Eastern Front in July and August 1943, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> attacked the Soviet salient around Kursk in Operation Citadel. Prepared Soviet defences halted the offensive within days, and Soviet counter-offensives retook Oryol and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kharkiv">Kharkov</a>. One of the largest battles in history, with great tank clashes such as Prokhorovka, it was the last major German offensive in the east.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kursk.jpg" alt="Battle of Kursk" width="320" height="490" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Kursk_(map).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
